    {
        "id": "comment-flex",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "example-flex-ops",
        "name": "Flex Operations Explained",
        "info": "## Flex Nodes Advantages:\n\n### Dynamic Configuration:\n- Change addresses at runtime\n- Modify function codes dynamically\n- Adjust quantity based on conditions\n\n### Use Cases:\n1. **Multi-device polling**: Different addresses for different devices\n2. **Conditional reads**: Read different registers based on state\n3. **Variable writes**: Write different values based on input\n4. **Custom protocols**: Implement vendor-specific function codes\n\n### Message Format:\n```javascript\nmsg.payload = {\n    fc: 3,        // Function code\n    unitid: 1,    // Unit/Slave ID\n    address: 100, // Starting address\n    quantity: 10, // Number of registers\n    value: []     // For write operations\n}\n```",
        "x": 190,
        "y": 40
    }
]